## Project Memory

Captured decisions and context for this repo. Generated by `whyanchor generate` — do not edit inside this block, it will be overwritten.

### architecture

- **Memory entries are markdown files with YAML frontmatter, one per file** (2026-09-21 · refs: src/core/schema.ts#MemoryFrontmatterSchema · tags: architecture, storage)
  Chosen over a single JSON or SQLite store so git handles merge, diff and blame for free. Small per-entry files also conflict far less than one shared file when two people capture at the same time, and they stay readable and editable in any editor without the tool installed. The schema lives in src/core/schema.ts and every read and write is validated against it, so a hand-edited entry fails loudly instead of silently corrupting the store.
- **Marker replacement is line-exact, shared by the memory and usage blocks** (2026-09-20 · refs: src/generators/agentsFile.ts#upsertMarkedSection · tags: architecture, generation)
  upsertMarkedSection replaces only the text between a start and end marker, matching each marker as a full line rather than a substring — an entry's rendered body can legitimately contain the literal marker text, and indexOf matched that instead of the real closing marker, truncating CLAUDE.md mid-sentence. Both CLAUDE.md blocks use it: the generated memory block (ctx-memory:start) and the agent usage block written by memory connect (ctx-memory:usage:start), which is why they can coexist and survive each other's regeneration. upsertMemorySection is now a thin wrapper kept for the existing call sites.
- **Fast-tier staleness uses git log + content hash, not an LLM** (2026-09-19 · refs: src/core/staleness.ts#checkRef · tags: architecture, staleness)
  memory check re-hashes each ref's symbol/file and counts commits touching that file since capture (src/core/staleness.ts). A hash mismatch is a high-confidence flag; commits with no hash change is low-confidence. Symbol extraction now searches up to 50 lines ahead for the opening brace (src/core/fingerprint.ts) so multi-line signatures fingerprint the whole body, not just the declaration line.

